          "path": "_m/x/n/7/s/ushiku-daibutsu-wp/ushiku-buddha-statue-parking-a.jpg",
          "filename": "Ushiku Buddha Statue Parking Area.jpg",
          "caption": "Ushiku Buddha Statue Parking Area \n Ushiku Amida-Buddha  statue also known as Ushiku Daibutsu (牛久大仏)  is located in  Ushiku City, |baraki Prefecture, Japan. Completed in 1993, the Buddha is 120 meters (390 feet) high and is three times as large as the Statue of Liberty[1]&gt;. This statue held the highest record of statues from 1993 to 2008. As of 2018, it is one of the five tallest statues in the world. \n\n&lt;Info&gt;  The name Amida[2]&gt; is an abbreviation for Amitabha[3]&gt;, which is a form often used in Japan.",
          "alt": "Ushiku Buddha Statue Parking Area \n Ushiku Amida-Buddha  statue also known as Ushiku Daibutsu (牛久大仏)  is located in  Ushiku City, |baraki Prefecture, Japan. Completed in 1993, the Buddha is 120 meters (390 feet) high and is three times as large as the Statue of Liberty[1]&gt;. This statue held the highest record of statues from 1993 to 2008. As of 2018, it is one of the five tallest statues in the world. \n\n&lt;Info&gt;  The name Amida[2]&gt; is an abbreviation for Amitabha[3]&gt;, which is a form often used in Japan.",
